@startuml
!theme plain
title Boat Rudder - Writing a comment from epoch 1 or 2

actor "Visitor\n(Netscape 3, IE 5...)" as Visitor
participant "http_router" as R
participant "comments" as COM
participant "captcha" as CAP
database "MongoDB" as DB
participant "mailer thread" as MAIL

== The entry page ==
Visitor -> R : GET /blog/<link>
R -> COM : comments_section(epoch 1/2)
COM -> CAP : captcha_new()\nanswer = HMAC(secret, nonce|issued)
CAP --> COM : token (no image)
COM --> Visitor : comments + form\n<img src="/comments/captcha?t=token">\n(no honeypot field)

== The image ==
Visitor -> R : GET /comments/captcha?t=token
R -> CAP : token's mac valid? age <= 15 min?
alt valid
  CAP -> CAP : answer from the token,\ndrawing seeded from it (same token, same image)
  CAP --> Visitor : 200 image/gif, no-store
else invalid / expired
  R --> Visitor : 404
end

== Sending ==
Visitor -> R : POST /blog/<link>/comments\n(Latin-1 or UTF-8)
R -> COM : comments_post()
COM -> COM : not UTF-8? read as Latin-1, convert
COM -> COM : same checks as epoch 3\n(challenge, 3 s, limits, name, block)
COM -> DB : store comment, queue confirmation email
COM --> Visitor : 302 /blog/<link>?comment=sent#comments
MAIL -> MAIL : sends it (unchanged)

@enduml
